=== QR001 | reverse asc is desc
r:{[p] reverse asc p}

=== QR001 | and reverse desc is asc
r:{[p] reverse desc p}

=== clean | reverse at a line's end is the function, and the next line a statement of its own (q 5, #730)
s:reverse
asc 3 1 2

=== QR001 | an indented line continues the statement
s:reverse
  asc 3 1 2

=== clean | under an iterator the sort is per item, and reverse reorders the items (q 5: reverse asc each (2 1;4 3) is (3 4;1 2), desc each is (2 1;4 3))
r1:{[p] reverse asc each p}
r2:{[p] reverse asc'[p]}
r3:{[p] reverse desc peach p}

=== clean | each over apply iterates too (#402; q 5: reverse asc@'x is per item, desc@'x is not the same)
r1:{[p] reverse asc@'p}
r2:{[p] reverse asc .'p}

=== clean | and so does one on the next line (q 5: reverse asc over   .'p is per item, desc .'p is not, #685)
r0:{[p] reverse asc
  .'p}
r1:{[p] distinct asc distinct
  .'p}
r2:{[p] reverse asc

  each p}

=== clean | first asc is not min: asc puts a null first and min skips it
r:{[p] first asc p}

=== QR002 | an identity lambda under each
r:{[p] {x} each p}

=== QR002 | spelled with the each adverb too
r:{[p] {x}'[p]}

=== clean | each-prior is something else
r:{[p] {x}':[p]}

=== QR003 | distinct after sorting distinct items
r:{[p] distinct asc distinct p}

=== clean | distinct at a line's end is the function, and the next line a statement of its own (q 5, #730)
d:distinct
asc distinct 1 1 2

=== clean | distinct each can make two items equal, which the outer distinct removes (q 5: (1 1 2;1 2) gives enlist 1 2, not two items)
r1:{[p] distinct asc distinct each p}
r2:{[p] distinct asc distinct'[p]}
r3:{[p] distinct asc distinct peach p}

=== clean | and so does each over apply (#402; q 5: distinct asc distinct@'(3 1 2;5 4;3 1 2) has two items, asc distinct@' three)
r1:{[p] distinct asc distinct@'p}
r2:{[p] distinct asc distinct .'p}

=== QR004 | one arithmetic operation with a number, which is atomic
r:{[p] {x+1} each p}

=== QR004 | the number on the left
r:{[p] {2*x} each p}

=== QR004 | a subtraction, spaced or not (q 5: {x-1} each (1 2;3 4) and {x - 1} each are both (0 1;2 3))
r1:{[p] {x-1} each p}
r2:{[p] {x - 1} each p}

=== clean | x indexed at a negative literal is not arithmetic (q 5: {x -1} each (1 2;3 4) is 0N 0N)
r:{[p] {x -1} each p}

=== clean | a lambda that is not one atomic operation needs its each
r1:{[p] {x,1} each p}
r3:{[p] {sum x} each p}

=== clean | sum is not +/: it skips nulls
r:{[p] {x+y}/[p]}
